        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 18. In the event there is a legitimate strike existing in a store or market of the Company, which has been called by a local union and authorized by its parent International Union and has been sanctioned by the International President of the Amalgamated Meat Cutters and Butcher Workmen of North America in Chicago, Illinois, members of the Union employed in the Company's store or market where such legitimate and authorized labor dispute is in progress, shall not be required to report for work, but shall not be entitled to pay for the days not so worked.",
            "block_bbox": [
