        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 19. TIME OFF IN CASE OF DEATH IN FAMILY. In the case of a death in the immediate family (namely, the death of a parent, spouse, child, brother, sister, mother-in-law or father-in-law) of a full time employee requiring the employee's absence from his regularly scheduled assignments, the employee shall be granted a leave of absence up to and including three (3) working days. Where the employee's normal time off falls within the three day period, he will be reimbursed at his basic straight-time rate for that portion of time normally scheduled for work but, under no circumstances, shall the application of this clause result in a change in the employee's basic weekly pay.",
